GATE="secrets"
EXPECT_EXIT="1"
EXPECT_RULE="private-key"
EXPECT_SCANNED_MIN="2"
DESCRIPTION="A planted private key PLUS a .gitleaksignore holding its fingerprint. This is the bypass that worked: gitleaks reads a suppression list from the repository under test, so committing one took the gate from fail-with-one-finding to pass-with-none while the denominator ROSE, because the suppressing commit is itself scanned work. Every integrity check held and the finding simply vanished. The rule asserted here is private-key, not the suppression-attempt rule, because the point is that the SECRET is still found -- a gate that only reported someone had tried to silence it would fail closed while telling you nothing about what leaked."
